---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Content Transparency"
  description="How Lythaus combines creator declarations, flags, and trained moderation review."
  canonicalPath="/ai-moderation"
>
  <section class="section">
    <h1>Content Transparency and Review</h1>
    <p>
      Lythaus launches with creator declarations, community flags, and staff
      review. Paid automated detection is not active.
    </p>

    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Creator declaration</strong> — each publishable post is labelled
        Human-authored or AI-assisted. Fully AI-generated content cannot be
        published; uncertain content remains Under review and non-public.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Community flags</strong> — members can report content that may
        violate policy.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Trained moderation review</strong> — flagged or uncertain
        content can be marked Under review and assessed under recorded policy.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Transparency</h2>
    <p>
      If your post is flagged, you will see the reason and can appeal. Our
      moderation console gives moderators full context before any action is
      taken.
    </p>

    <h2>Appeals</h2>
    <p>
      Eligible appeals are reviewed by five independently assigned trained
      reviewers. A trained adjudicator confirms the outcome; high-risk cases
      require two independent adjudications. There is no community voting or
      time-based automatic resolution.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
